{"vid":"XLKXcrfLxwg","source":"XLKXcrfLxwg.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"When you're not a native speaker of"},{"t":1.9,"txt":"English and you want an American accent,"},{"t":3.9,"txt":"[clears throat]"},{"t":4.8,"txt":"it's important to really understand the"},{"t":7.2,"txt":"rhythm and melody of American English"},{"t":10,"txt":"along with the individual sounds. Today,"},{"t":12.9,"txt":"we're going to focus in on one sound and"},{"t":15.2,"txt":"how to master it, the L. I'm Rachel. I"},{"t":18.4,"txt":"have a background in opera singing and"},{"t":20.7,"txt":"I've been teaching the American accent"},{"t":22.7,"txt":"for over 20 years. I've developed an"},{"t":25.6,"txt":"extremely effective method for mastering"},{"t":28.4,"txt":"the American accent. You can learn about"},{"t":30.9,"txt":"it and sign up for my courses at"},{"t":33.4,"txt":"rachelsenglishacademy.com."},{"t":36,"txt":"Join over 50,000 students who are now"},{"t":39.3,"txt":"speaking English with confidence."},{"t":42,"txt":"Let's look at an L that begins a word."},{"t":45.3,"txt":"There are two different tongue positions"},{"t":47.3,"txt":"you can use. Let's compare the L"},{"t":49.6,"txt":"position with the mouth at rest on the"},{"t":51.7,"txt":"left. First, your tongue tip can be"},{"t":54.6,"txt":"lifted. Where exactly the tongue tip is"},{"t":57.8,"txt":"can vary a little bit. It can be"},{"t":60,"txt":"touching the very forward part of the"},{"t":62.3,"txt":"roof of the mouth. It can be touching"},{"t":64.6,"txt":"where the roof of the mouth and the"},{"t":66.1,"txt":"teeth meet, or it can be touching the"},{"t":68.6,"txt":"backs of the teeth. If you've studied"},{"t":71.4,"txt":"pronunciation before, you've probably"},{"t":73.8,"txt":"learned that this is the position of the"},{"t":76,"txt":"tongue for the L sound. But, there is"},{"t":78.8,"txt":"another common position that makes the"},{"t":81.2,"txt":"same sound. I notice I do this a lot."},{"t":84.2,"txt":"For this other position, the tongue"},{"t":86.1,"txt":"comes through the teeth. They both sound"},{"t":88.6,"txt":"the same and they're interchangeable."},{"t":91,"txt":"Here's the first way to make the light L"},{"t":93.2,"txt":"with the tongue tip going to the roof of"},{"t":94.7,"txt":"the mouth, and here's the second way to"},{"t":96.7,"txt":"make it with the tongue tip coming"},{"t":98.4,"txt":"through the teeth. Two different"},{"t":100.5,"txt":"positions that make the same sound."},{"t":103.2,"txt":"Let's watch the word lack up close and"},{"t":107.2,"txt":"in slow motion. You can see the tongue"},{"t":109.6,"txt":"tip comes through the teeth."},{"t":113.2,"txt":"lack"},{"t":117.7,"txt":"The L is also common in a beginning"},{"t":120.2,"txt":"cluster or blend. We have BL like blind."},{"t":125.3,"txt":">> blind"},{"t":129.6,"txt":">> We have CL like clap."},{"t":134.5,"txt":">> clap"},{"t":138.2,"txt":">> We have FL like"},{"t":140.5,"txt":"flame."},{"t":143.5,"txt":">> flame"},{"t":146.8,"txt":">> We have GL like glass."},{"t":151.2,"txt":">> glass"},{"t":155.9,"txt":">> We have PL like plants."},{"t":159.9,"txt":">> plants"},{"t":164,"txt":">> We have SL like slow."},{"t":168.2,"txt":">> slow"},{"t":171.9,"txt":">> Let's practice a little bit. The word"},{"t":174.4,"txt":"let's starts with an L. Let's."},{"t":177.9,"txt":"Let's. I notice I'm bringing my tongue"},{"t":180.5,"txt":"tip through the teeth for that. Let's."},{"t":183.8,"txt":"Let's."},{"t":186.8,"txt":"You pick a position that feels the most"},{"t":189,"txt":"comfortable for you."},{"t":190.6,"txt":"Let's."},{"t":191.8,"txt":"Let's practice."},{"t":195.3,"txt":">> Let's."},{"t":200.1,"txt":"blind"},{"t":206.3,"txt":">> [sighs]"},{"t":206.5,"txt":">> clap"},{"t":211.6,"txt":"flame"},{"t":215.5,"txt":"glass"},{"t":221.1,"txt":"plants"},{"t":225.3,"txt":">> So now you've learned the two positions"},{"t":228.2,"txt":"for an L when it begins a word or is"},{"t":231,"txt":"part of a beginning blend or cluster."},{"t":234,"txt":"What about at the end of a word?"},{"t":236.4,"txt":"What about the L in the middle of a"},{"t":238.2,"txt":"word? Yes, that can be completely"},{"t":240.7,"txt":"different. The L you've just learned is"},{"t":243.5,"txt":"called the light L. But we also have an"},{"t":246.6,"txt":"L called a dark L. When you look up a"},{"t":249.4,"txt":"word in the dictionary and you look at"},{"t":251.4,"txt":"the pronunciation, it will not tell you"},{"t":254.2,"txt":"if it's a light L or a dark L. You'll"},{"t":256.5,"txt":"only see one symbol, this, no matter if"},{"t":260,"txt":"it's in the word lack, class, feel, or"},{"t":263.4,"txt":"walls."},{"t":264.6,"txt":"Here's the rule. An L is a light L if it"},{"t":268,"txt":"comes before the vowel or diphthong"},{"t":270.2,"txt":"sound in a syllable. So, any L at the"},{"t":273.5,"txt":"beginning of a word or in a beginning"},{"t":275.6,"txt":"blend, like we studied, but also any L"},{"t":279.1,"txt":"within a word that comes before a vowel"},{"t":282,"txt":"or diphthong in that syllable. For"},{"t":284.4,"txt":"example, the word ungluing."},{"t":286.9,"txt":"The L isn't at the beginning of the"},{"t":288.6,"txt":"word, which is always a light L, and it"},{"t":290.9,"txt":"isn't at the end of the word, which is"},{"t":292.6,"txt":"always a dark L, but let's look at the"},{"t":295.1,"txt":"breakdown of the syllables. There are"},{"t":297.5,"txt":"three. un"},{"t":299.5,"txt":"glu ing"},{"t":301.3,"txt":"Look at the syllable with the L. Does it"},{"t":303.6,"txt":"come before or after the vowel in that"},{"t":306.2,"txt":"syllable? It comes before the oo vowel."},{"t":309.5,"txt":"It's a light L. Ungluing."},{"t":312.4,"txt":"Ungluing. un glu I'm making that by"},{"t":316.3,"txt":"lifting my tongue tip up. ungluing"},{"t":320.4,"txt":"ungluing I'm touching the backs of my"},{"t":323.1,"txt":"top front teeth. ungluing What about the"},{"t":326.2,"txt":"word believe?"},{"t":328.2,"txt":"Let's look at the syllable breakdown"},{"t":329.8,"txt":"again. It's in the middle of the word,"},{"t":332.1,"txt":"but at the beginning of the syllable."},{"t":334.1,"txt":"That's a light L. I have the phrase"},{"t":337.2,"txt":"believe me here. Let's look at that up"},{"t":339.9,"txt":"close and in slow motion."},{"t":342.9,"txt":"believe"},{"t":345,"txt":"me"},{"t":347.1,"txt":"You can see the tongue tip comes through"},{"t":349.2,"txt":"the teeth."},{"t":350.3,"txt":"One of our two positions for the light"},{"t":352.2,"txt":"L."},{"t":353.1,"txt":"Let's look at all the light L words"},{"t":355.6,"txt":"we've studied one more time."},{"t":359.8,"txt":">> black"},{"t":364.7,"txt":"blind"},{"t":370.5,"txt":"claw"},{"t":376.2,"txt":"flame"},{"t":380.1,"txt":"glass"},{"t":385.7,"txt":"plant"},{"t":389.7,"txt":">> Now, I'm not going to lie, the dark L is"},{"t":392.6,"txt":"one of the hardest sounds for my"},{"t":394.5,"txt":"students to get. I'm not even going to"},{"t":396.6,"txt":"try to tackle that in this video. It"},{"t":399.3,"txt":"will be the next one that comes out on"},{"t":401.1,"txt":"my channel, so be sure to subscribe with"},{"t":403.5,"txt":"notifications on. Once my students"},{"t":406.4,"txt":"master the dark L, they speak with such"},{"t":409.1,"txt":"a natural overall sound. It's definitely"},{"t":412.2,"txt":"worth putting in the effort to learn it."},{"t":415.4,"txt":"Keep your learning going now with this"},{"t":417.2,"txt":"video, and don't forget to check out"},{"t":419.4,"txt":"rachelsenglishacademy.com"},{"t":421.8,"txt":"to learn more about my American accent"},{"t":424.2,"txt":"training courses that can help you"},{"t":426.2,"txt":"develop a truly American voice. That's"},{"t":429.3,"txt":"it, and thanks so much for using"},{"t":431.6,"txt":"Rachel's English."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"When"},{"t":0.44,"w":"you're"},{"t":0.64,"w":"not"},{"t":0.92,"w":"a"},{"t":1,"w":"native"},{"t":1.4,"w":"speaker"},{"t":1.8,"w":"of"},{"t":1.92,"w":"English"},{"t":2.52,"w":"and"},{"t":2.68,"w":